.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.axiom/
# Everything under data/ is a rebuildable artifact -- model exports, HF cache,
# embedding caches, eval runs -- except the sweep evidence. A tuned constant in
# config.py cites its sweep JSON by path (RESOLVED_PLACEHOLDERS), so that file
# has to be in the repo or the citation points at nothing a reviewer can open.
#
# The four lines are load-bearing in this order: git never descends into an
# excluded *directory*, so a bare `data/` makes the `!data/sweeps/*.json`
# negation below unreachable and new evidence can only be added with
# `git add -f`, which Rules.md section 9.5 forbids. Excluding the directory's
# *contents* (`data/*`) instead leaves the door open for the negations.
#
# Scoped to `oq*.json` rather than `*.json`: the evidence files are a few KB
# each and named for the question they answer, while a per-query predictions
# dump landing in the same directory is 13 MB of rebuildable output. Matching
# the naming convention keeps the rule from silently committing the latter.
data/*
!data/sweeps/
data/sweeps/*
!data/sweeps/oq*.json
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.env
models/
*.onnx
*.gguf
# The MTEB submission artifact. It is ignored by default because intermediate
# runs land here, but the ONE that ships must be committable -- Deployment.md
# section 4.2 step 3 does `git add appsretrieval_results.json`, and Rules.md
# section 9.5 forbids `git add -f`. The negation below is what makes that work.
appsretrieval_results.json
!appsretrieval_results.json
.axiom*/
